import{_ as t,o as a,c as o,ai as s}from"./chunks/framework.Cabe_Szf.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"GPU map","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/guide/gpu-map.md","filePath":"en/guide/gpu-map.md","lastUpdated":1792109577000}'),r={name:"en/guide/gpu-map.md"};function i(n,e,h,d,l,m){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="gpu-map" tabindex="-1">GPU map <a class="header-anchor" href="#gpu-map" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;GPU map&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The <strong>GPU map</strong> shows what sits in video memory right now, model by model, what each one&#39;s context costs on top of its weights, what is free, and which of your other models would fit.</p><p><strong>Sidebar item:</strong> GPU map (below Shared box) <strong>Route:</strong> <code>/gpu</code><strong>Added in:</strong> v0.8.0 (October 2026) <strong>Requires:</strong> nothing extra. It reads Ollama&#39;s own report of loaded models every few seconds. The card&#39;s memory size comes from the NVIDIA driver on Windows and Linux, and from the system on macOS.</p><h2 id="what-s-the-point" tabindex="-1">What&#39;s the point? <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-s-the-point" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What&#39;s the point?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Will it fit&quot; is the question in every local-model thread, and the answer is usually a number from <code>nvidia-smi</code> that nobody can read. The map draws it.</p><h2 id="the-bar" tabindex="-1">The bar <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-bar" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The bar&quot;">​</a></h2><p>One bar, the width of the card&#39;s video memory. A block per loaded model, split in two: the weights, and dimmer, what the context and working buffers cost on top. Then the free space. Hover any block for its size.</p><p>Under the bar, each loaded model with its size, its quantisation, the context it is loaded with, and when the daemon will unload it unless it is used again. A model that did not fit shows how much of it runs from system RAM instead, which is why it is slow.</p><h2 id="what-else-would-fit" tabindex="-1">What else would fit <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-else-would-fit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What else would fit&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every pulled model that is not loaded, against the free space, with one of three verdicts:</p><ul><li><strong>fits now</strong>, next to what is loaded;</li><li><strong>fits only if what is loaded unloads first</strong>;</li><li><strong>larger than this card</strong>: it would run partly from system RAM.</li></ul><p>A model needs about 15% more than its file for a modest context; the verdicts allow for that.</p><h2 id="what-the-page-does-not-know" tabindex="-1">What the page does not know <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-page-does-not-know" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What the page does not know&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How the daemon splits one model&#39;s footprint between weights and context. The weights are the file on disk; the rest is the context&#39;s cache and working buffers, so that split is an estimate. Free space is the card&#39;s memory minus what Ollama reports loaded; other programs using the GPU are not counted.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="./system.html">My System</a> for the card and the driver.</li><li><a href="./shared-box.html">Shared box</a> for which tool reserved the context.</li></ul>',16)])])}const u=t(r,[["render",i]]);export{c as __pageData,u as default};
